  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Specific Action on the Provision of Services to Victims of Trafficking in Human Beings Who Are Third-Country Nationals</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project foresees a series to enhance the knowledge and skills of trainings for front-line staff working at reception facilities, shelters, or other specialized facilities aiming to equip them with necessary competencies that wouldin order to allow them to address VoT protection needs in an appropriate and effective manner and to prevent exploitation. In addition, Further activities will take place aiming to empower VoT based on their individualized needs. VoT&#x2019;s efforts to integrate into the Greek community, and in particular access educational, employability, vocational training and other integration opportunities, will be facilitated empowered through the provision of in-kind support, aiming to help them access educational, employability, vocational training and other integration opportunities. Moreover, the living conditions for VoTs accommodated in shelters, sites and other facilities assisting VoT will be provided improved through with a needs-based approach depending on the facility, support including the provision of equipment in line with their needs that will enable them to improve their living conditions. Finally, EKKA&#x2019;s capacity and specifically the counter-trafficking activities under the National Referral Mechanism (NRM) will be enhanced through will receive technical support through via the appointment of experts. supporting counter-trafficking activities under the National Referral Mechanism (NRM).</narrative>
  </description>
